A contract of lease is not terminated either by the death of the lessor or of the lessee. In the event of the death of the lessee, however, his heirs may claim the termination of the lease if they establish that, as a result of the death of the person whose estate they inherited, the burden of the lease has become too heavy for their resources or that the lease exceeds their needs. In such an event, the periods of notice of termination laid down in Article 563 shall be observed and the claim for termination of the lease made within six months at the most from the date of death of the lessee.
